Add dtiMerge, a CLI for merging checkpoints and LoRAs

The model mixing UI is in the macOS app, but there are some surviving parts in
the community tree.  LoRALoader.mergeLoRA supplies the arithmetic unchanged.
That's a function of name, dataType and shape, so we can drive it from a store's
own key list without need a model graph, and LoRAImporter has already folded
alpha over rank into the stored factors, which leaves strength a plain scalar.

Quantized and ezm7 inputs are promoted, dtypes are preserved per tensor because
ccv_nnc_tensor_read cannot convert 16F to 16BF and LTX-2.3 carries four 16BF
tensors inside an otherwise f16 conversion.  Shapes reconcile as squeezed, since
a q6p conversion writes[1, 1, 1, 128] where the f16 one writes [128].
